yne that offers surround-view lidar sensors comprising VLP-16, VLP-16 Lite, VLP-16 Hi-Res, VLP-32, and VLS-128; Ouster Gemini, a perception platform designed for smart infrastructure deployments; and BlueCity, a Gemini-powered solution for traffic operations, planning, and safety. In addition, the company offers ZED, a high-performance camera that provides 2D and 3D color data, as well as AI Compute. Further, it is developing solid-state digital flash sensors, a suite of short, mid, and long-range solid-state digital lidar sensors that provide uniform precision imaging without motion blur across an entire field of view. Ouster, Inc. was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles Angus Pacala | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 36 | Compensation: $893,600 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 320 people. Revenue per employee of $529K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 50%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $128K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Ouster, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.4B market cap on $169M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +60% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -248% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 27%.","The company is burning through $65M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 24% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 50% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 361% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster tha